#
# aria2c deliverable — handed in as a binary artifact.
# NOT downloaded. NOT built during a normal IRIS build.
#
# Rebuilt 2026-09-10 with tools/aria2c-build/ and patches 0001 through 0007.
# Adds the seeder good-bye grace (#68): a seeder<->seeder connection now
# survives 5 s past completion on both ends, so the device's
# --on-bt-download-complete hook can still read per-peer bytes over RPC.
# Retains the hard peer admission cap (#168), coalesced-handshake
# preservation (#174) and OpenSSL 3.5.8; same pinned toolchain as before.
# Validated via wire/RPC regressions, real BitTorrent transfers and the
# loopback grace check described in tools/aria2c-build/README.md.
# Execution: native x86_64; aarch64 under QEMU.
#
# aria2-next version : 2.5.6
# source pin         : d4971f0e12322e2ffcdb1721911b7d5c6206d0e5
# patches applied    : 7
#   - 0001-getpeers-keys-filter.patch
#   - 0002-fix-uaf-peer-blocklist-disconnect.patch
#   - 0003-fix-pkcs12-chain-type-confusion.patch
#   - 0004-fix-ed2k-iterator-invalidation.patch
#   - 0005-hard-bt-max-peers.patch
#   - 0006-preserve-coalesced-bt-handshake.patch
#   - 0007-seeder-goodbye-grace.patch
#
# tools/get-aria2c.sh verifies the handed-in binary against these
# checksums and FAILS CLOSED on a mismatch, so a stale client cannot
# silently ship. Update this file only when adopting a new build.
